cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this firmware or its ideas, please cite it as below."
title: "Shramko Motor Autostart: Betaflight firmware that spins a motor on power-up without a receiver"
abstract: "A small module for Betaflight 2025.12.1 that turns a flight controller into a standalone motor driver: after power-on it waits a configurable delay, ramps the ESC linearly to a configurable throttle over a configurable time and holds it - no transmitter, receiver or switch. Optional momentary button on two pads (internal pull-up), optional RC receiver / AUX switch, DShot or PWM, all settings in the Betaflight CLI. Firmware 1.1 adds a LiPo cut-off, a run time, a throttle limit and random gusts; a web configurator edits the settings over Web Serial, and an agent protocol builds the firmware for other boards with the reference setup."
